      "description": "Watch Wigan Athletic vs Milton Keynes Dons highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as Wigan Athletic hosted Milton Keynes Dons in a highly anticipated League One encounter on September 2, 2026. Both sides took to the pitch with ambitious tactical setups, promising a high-intensity battle from the very first whistle. Early Intensity and the Opening Strike The match began with a series of physical challenges, leading to early yellow cards for Finley Burns and Jack Sanders as both teams fought for midfield supremacy. Wigan had to adapt early when Luke Harris was forced off, replaced by Reggie Walsh in the 22nd minute. Despite the disruption, the home side broke the deadlock in the 36th minute. A clinical piece of play saw Max Power provide a perfect assist for Jensen Weir , who fired home to give the Latics the lead. Building Momentum After the Break Wigan Athletic wasted no time asserting their authority in the second half. Just three minutes after the restart, in the 48th minute, the roles shifted as the creator became the scorer; Max Power found the back of the net to double the advantage. MK Dons attempted to find a way back into the game with a flurry of substitutions, including the introduction of Alex Gilbey and Marvin Ekpiteta , but the home defense remained resolute under pressure. Closing Out a Dominant Victory The final stages of the match saw the home side capitalize on their momentum. In the 74th minute, fresh off the bench, Bradley Burrowes made an immediate impact by setting up Jensen Weir for his second goal of the afternoon. The rout was completed in the 81st minute when Aaron Collins struck the fourth, leaving no doubt about the result. When the final whistle blew after seven minutes of stoppage time, it confirmed a comprehensive and professional performance from a clinical Wigan side."
